  "context": "Found by the independent review of #145 (Optional). Guardrail: do not loosen bundle:fetch or bundle:verify for ordinary bundles.\n\nReview 2026-11-13. Decision gate: choose between (A) certify the --from directory now and (B) remove --from. Default is A, because it does not wait on anything; B is allowed only after first-default-docs-pin-run is done, since until then --from is the only way to reproduce the v0.5.0 pin. Record the choice and reason here before coding. Verification rubric for A: the three refusal tests in acceptance, plus a manual run of `npm run docs:pin -- v0.5.0 --from <v0.5.0 bundle dir>` that either reproduces release-pin/ byte for byte (`git status --short release-pin` empty) or is refused for a stated reason that the owner accepts. Guardrails: bundle:fetch and bundle:verify behaviour for ordinary bundles is unchanged (their test files pass unmodified); scripts/schemas is not loosened; no network call is added to `--check --offline`.\n\nOwner decision 2026-11-14: option A, certify the --from directory (manifest, attestations, online certification); skip only member schema validation. Merge targets (owner, 2026-11-14): site code, workflows and corrections to released documentation go to main on green ci, then main is merged into next; only documentation of unreleased behaviour waits on next.",
  "description": "Problem: `npm run docs:pin -- vX.Y.Z --from <dir>` accepts any directory whose manifest core_sha, package_version and three member digests agree with each other and with the tag. It runs no attestation or certification check, so a hand-assembled directory can be pinned, and the pin's `--check` cannot tell. It exists because the v0.5.0 bundle fails the current doc-contracts schema. Outcome: a pin can only come from a bundle that core certified.\n\nOptions to choose between: run the manifest, attestation and online certification checks on the `--from` directory while skipping only the member schema validation the old bundle fails; or remove `--from` once a release newer than v0.5.0 is pinned and no old bundle needs it.",
